    "pressure": {
      "file": "laser_alignment_equipment_pressure.glb",
      "title": "The beam spot reveals misalignment",
      "description": "Each unit projects a laser onto the opposite unit's position detector (PSD). As both shafts are turned together through at least ≈ 70–140° (e.g. 9-12-3 o'clock), the spot traces a path whose movement gives offset and angularity in both planes. The display calculates shim values and horizontal moves for each motor foot and can update live while moving. Advantages over dial indicators: no bracket sag, higher resolution (≈ 1 µm), faster. Check soft foot first and apply thermal-growth targets.",
      "render": "normal",
      "annotations": []
    }
  },
